% SLIDE 12. 28-31. Supplied SymbolTable API names are exact.
### Initializer Before New Binding
Parsing: `double x = expression;`
...
[pseudo] @(70,220) {$code, w=790px, size=24px} ```text
read type, name, and '='
initializer = parse the expression
require ';'
id = symbols.DeclareVariable(name_token)
     build Declaration(id, initializer)
```
...
[order] @(905,225) {$note, w=295px} Registering x too early would make its initializer read the new zero-valued local.
...
[errors] @(70,430) {$note} Without a visible outer x, `double x = x + 1;` is an unknown-name error. Every declaration requires an initializer.
[sharing] @(70,545) {$note} Parameters and the outer function body share a scope. A local cannot redeclare a parameter there. Nested braces may shadow it.
