% SLIDE 13. 31-34. Make the parser/storage distinction concrete.
### Stable IDs Survive Scope Exit
[pseudo] @(70,150) {$code, w=750px, size=25px} ```text
Enter function:
    create SymbolTable(program, function_id)
    declare parameters in its initial scope

Enter nested braces: PushScope()
Resolve a reference:  LookupVariable(token)
Leave nested braces: PopScope()
```
[retained] @(865,155) {$note, w=335px} Pop removes visibility. The variable record and its numeric ID remain available to the translator.
...
[function] @(70,465) {$note, w=1035px, color=emp} `FunctionInfo` must retain ordered `parameter_ids`, `local_ids`, and a body AST.
...
[storage] @(70,530) {$note} Emit all parameter and local declarations before instructions. Use IDs for WAT names such as `$var0`, even when source spellings repeat.
...
[lifetime] @(70,640) {$note, size=24px, color=focus} Keep IDs across vector growth. References to vector elements can become invalid after push_back.
---
% SLIDE 14. 34-37. Answers: Skipped(0)=0, Skipped(1)=7, Skipped(0)=0 again.
### Local Storage and Declaration Execution
[source] @(70,150) {$code, w=750px, size=25px} ```cpp
function Skipped(double flag) : double {
  if (flag) double x = 7;
  return x;
}
```
...
[q] @(865,160) {$note, w=335px, color=focus} Predict Skipped(0), Skipped(1), then Skipped(0) again on the same instance.
...
[answer] @(865,350) {$note, w=335px, color=emp} 0, 7, 0. Each call starts with fresh locals initialized to zero.
...
[scope] @(70,395) {$note, w=750px} Only braces introduce scopes. This unbraced declaration belongs to the surrounding function scope.
...
[runtime] @(70,550) {$note} Declare storage at function entry. Execute the initializer at its original position, only when control reaches the declaration.
