% SLIDE 15. 37-40. ResetLocal(3)=3. Wrongly hoisted initializer yields 6.
### A Loop Runs Its Initializer Each Time
[source] @(70,150) {$code, w=750px, size=24px} ```cpp
function ResetLocal(double n) : double {
  double sum = 0;
  while (n > 0) {
    double t = 0;
    t = t + 1;
    sum = sum + t;
    n = n - 1;
  }
  return sum;
}
```
...
[predict] @(865,155) {$note, w=335px, color=focus} What does ResetLocal(3) return? What if t's initializer is moved before the loop?
...
[answer] @(865,365) {$note, w=335px, color=emp} Correct: 3. Moving the initializer before the loop makes the sum 1 + 2 + 3 = 6.
...
[distinction] @(70,550) {$note, size=27px} The local declaration appears in the WAT header. The initialization instructions remain inside the loop body.
---
% SLIDE 16. 40-42. The code is a legal fragment within a function.
### Small Statement Rules That Affect the AST
[source] @(70,150) {$code, w=750px, size=25px} ```cpp
if (a)
  if (b) x = 1;
  else x = 2;
{}
;
return x;
```
...
[else] @(865,155) {$note, w=335px} The else attaches to the nearest unmatched if. Parse its then statement recursively before looking for else.
...
[empty] @(70,410) {$note, w=1000px, color=emp} Accept empty statements and empty nested blocks. Neither leaves a value.
...
[rules] @(70,475) {$note} Reject nested function definitions and top-level statements. Parse the whole file, including input after the last valid function.
---
% SLIDE 17. 42-45. Implementation checklist; lexer code is supplied.
### Lexer Boundaries and Source Locations
[valid] @(70,175) {$code, w=750px, size=25px} ```text
Legal:    42   1_000   0x2A   1_000.25
Invalid:  .5   5.     1e3    1__0
```
[validate] @(70,325) {$note} Reject bad bytes, malformed literals, invalid tokens, and unterminated comments. Keep each token's original line for diagnostics.
...
[lifetime] @(70,450) {$note} `Lexer::Tokenize` returns its token vector by reference. Copy it or retain and use the lexer object. If using a copied vector, handle EOF explicitly.
...
[error] @(70,580) {$note, color=emp} Use `ReportError(token, message)`. The lexer's Error / checked Use helpers use a different diagnostic format.
---
% SLIDE 18. 45-48. This is a complete intentionally invalid program.
### Unreachable Source Still Needs Checking
[invalid] @(70,150) {$code, w=750px, size=25px} ```cpp
// INVALID source
function Bad() : double {
  return 1;
  return missing;
}
```
[q] @(865,160) {$note, w=335px, color=focus} The first return always runs. Can the compiler accept this function?
...
[answer] @(70,365) {$note, w=800px, color=emp} No. Resolve and validate the second return's expression too. Report the unknown name on line 4.
...
[traversal] @(70,470) {$note, w=750px} Parsing and semantic traversal inspect every source node. Runtime reachability is not even analyzed until semantic checking.
...
[final] @(70,620) {$note, size=27px} Also check the final direct return and loop context in every function. Reset loop depth between functions.
