% SLIDE 19. 48-50. Driver already implements this ordering.
### A Failed Compilation Produces No WAT
[pipeline] @(70,150) {$code, w=1140px, size=24px} ```text
Parse the complete Program
Analyze every function
Generate the complete module string
Write the module to stdout
```
...
[invalid] @(70,370) {$note} Invalid source requires exit status 1, empty stdout, and `ERROR (line N): useful explanation` on stderr.
...
[late] @(70,495) {$note} A valid first function followed by an invalid second function must still produce no WAT.{{br}}{{color=explain|Lexing}}, {{color=explain|Parsing}}, and {{color=explain|Semantic analysis}} should catch all errors.  THEN {{color=explain|code generation}} should be guaranteed to NOT produce errors.
...
[debug] @(70,640) {$note, size=25px, color=id} `./Project3 --ast file.strix > file.wat 2> file.log` keeps AST debugging out of WAT. The supplied driver prints ASTs after semantic checking succeeds.
