% SLIDE 21. 54-57. Students can use these sources as original regression seeds.
### Small Tests That Distinguish Bugs
[tests] @(70,155) {$code, w=1140px, size=24px} ```text
Chain():        a = b = 7; return a + b;          expect 14
Order():        return (x = 2) - (x = 5);         expect -3
LeftRead():     x starts at 10; return x-(x=2);   expect 8
ScopeExample(): outer x survives shadowing        expect 10
ResetLocal(3):  initializer executes each time    expect 3
Skipped(0), Skipped(1), Skipped(0):               expect 0,7,0
```
...
[why] @(70,435) {$note} Choose inputs that expose the rule. `x + 0` hides operand reversal. Repeated calls expose accidental state that survives function calls.
...
[files] @(70,555) {$note, color=emp} [Expression examples](Lecture14/expressions.strix) and [scope examples](Lecture14/scopes.strix) are ready to compile. The companion runner checks exports and source errors.
