### Exit Questions
[q1] @(70,155) {$note} Why does assignment need to preserve a value even when most assignments appear as statements?
...
[q2] @(70,290) {$note} Why can a compiler move local declarations to the function header while keeping their initializer instructions inside a loop?
...
[q3] @(70,425) {$note} Your compiler emits valid WAT but Order() returns the wrong result. Which evidence will you inspect next?
...
[answers] @(70,565) {$note, size=27px, color=emp} Assignment can feed a larger expression. Storage and initialization have different roles. Inspect the AST and the order of emitted operand code, then run a small distinguishing test.
